p2pool: fork 14 (block major version 7, version-2 coinbase with view tags)

Base: kryptokrona/p2pool 8edf632fae7ebcbb29d3525144ac77b0dbd6477e with
0001-fork13-v6.patch applied. Apply with `patch -p1 < 0002-fork14-tx-v2-coinbase.patch`.
Specification: docs/tx-v2.md (sections 2, 3, 5) in the xkr repository.

* coin_config.h: XKR_FORK14_HEIGHT (compile-time, default 3000000 = xkrd's provisional
  FORK_14_HEIGHT_MAINNET), FORK14_MAJOR_VERSION = 7, COINBASE_TX_VERSION_2,
  coinbase_tx_version(major), SUPPORTED_FORK_INDEX = 14 (signals forks 13 and 14).
* SideChain::network_major_version / configure_forks: major version 7 from block F + 1 on,
  XKR_FORK14_HEIGHT from the environment against a testnet daemon.
* xkr_serialize_real_coinbase (pool_block.cpp; used for the submitted block, the PoW blob,
  the coinbase hash, the aux header hash, the sidechain id and the tx key seed): for major
  version >= 7 the coinbase is version 2 and every output is `varint amount, 0x03, key[32],
  view_tag`. The view tag is the one create_miner_tx already derives next to the one-time
  key (Wallet::get_eph_public_key -> generate_key_derivation -> derive_view_tag, i.e.
  cn_fast_hash("view_tag" || 8rA || varint(i))[0], byte for byte xkr_crypto::view_tag).
* PoolBlock::deserialize: coinbase version 1 with 0x02 outputs below major 7, exactly
  version 2 with 0x03 outputs and a view tag from major 7 on (the same binding as
  xkr-serialization and the consensus coinbase rule).
* SideChain::verify: from major 7 on a share whose view tag differs from the payee's is
  invalid (a wrong tag would hide the output from tag-aware wallets).
* Below the fork-14 height every byte is unchanged.

